1
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,110
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:11,190
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:14,890
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:17,770
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:21,940
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:29,420
Certainly, thank you.

7
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:38,460
Excuse me, let me pass, please.

8
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,420
Raise your glass!

9
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:42,590
Please, make way...

10
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:48,770
Griffith...

11
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:13,560
Griffith!

12
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,530
Feel no shame about shape

13
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:38,450
Weather changes their phrase

14
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:42,200
Even mother will show you another way

15
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,580
So put your glasses on

16
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,660
Nothing will be wrong

17
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:48,870
There's no blame. There's no fame

18
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:50,710
It's up to you

19
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:54,340
The first words should be found

20
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:57,970
Whatever holds you back

21
00:01:58,840 --> 00:01:59,340
I...

22
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:00,470
...can...

23
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:02,640
I can get it off

24
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:03,640
Tell me what...

25
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,640
Tell me what...

26
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,480
Tell me what you want

27
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:07,560
I don't know why...

28
00:02:07,770 --> 00:02:08,560
Don't know why...

29
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,560
Don't know why you're afraid

30
00:02:10,730 --> 00:02:11,730
Tell me what...

31
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:12,690
Tell me what...

32
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:14,360
Tell me what you'd say

33
00:02:14,610 --> 00:02:15,690
I don't know why...

34
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:16,780
Don't know why...

35
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:17,570
Too late...

36
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:19,200
It's too late

37
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:28,120
Tombstone of Flames

38
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:35,590
Griffith!

39
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:37,420
Griffith!

40
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:38,300
Griffith!

41
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:48,640
Sentry, close down the hall!

42
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,230
Don't allow anyone to leave here!

43
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:04,990
Griffith!

44
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:06,290
Griffith!

45
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:08,290
Griffith!

46
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:21,380
How easy can this be?

47
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:24,390
Just think, I'll be making
a fortune off this ruse...

48
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:27,560
More than I could ever make
even after ten years of honest toil!

49
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:30,480
All I have to do is leave town by dawn...

50
00:04:02,130 --> 00:04:05,050
Who knew things would go so smoothly?

51
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:06,760
It's almost anticlimactic!

52
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,260
Indeed...

53
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:12,180
And we owe it all to Minister Foss,
for plotting such a brilliant scheme!

54
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:14,850
Truly, your expertise is to be commended!

55
00:04:14,850 --> 00:04:17,110
No, you're too kind.

56
00:04:17,650 --> 00:04:20,360
Well done, Minister Foss.

57
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:22,780
It is very kind of Your Majesty.

58
00:04:23,450 --> 00:04:24,700
What's the matter?

59
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:26,660
You do not look well.

60
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:29,330
I'm sure it's just your imagination.

61
00:04:29,330 --> 00:04:31,450
It's because you're
seeing me under candlelight.

62
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:35,170
Anyway, are you really sure
everything's going to be fine?

63
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:39,380
Because if that waiter is ever apprehended...

64
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:41,460
...and he ends up confessing...

65
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,680
Our names could very well be revealed!

66
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:47,800
No need to worry about that, gentlemen.

67
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:51,680
I just received word from
the operative I sent in beforehand...

68
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:54,690
...that the matter has
already been dealt with.

69
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:58,810
Oh, there is no detail
that escapes your guile!

70
00:04:58,810 --> 00:05:01,320
Really, you are quite the strategist!

71
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:03,570
Your talents are being
wasted as a mere minister!

72
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:09,780
Now then, if you would allow me
to go check on the state of the uproar...

73
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:30,050
At last, dignity will be
restored to the army of Midland.

74
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:31,720
That is certain.

75
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:35,680
It is ridiculous that a mere mercenary
could become White Hawk General!

76
00:05:36,230 --> 00:05:38,850
His example would
have put all kinds of ideas...

77
00:05:38,850 --> 00:05:41,440
...into the heads of common soldiers.

78
00:05:41,770 --> 00:05:44,320
We of noble blood,
and no one else, should be...

79
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:48,160
...the ones to assume the pivotal
roles in our kingdom's administration.

80
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:50,820
How could that man
of lowly birth presume to...

81
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:54,330
Inferior subjects have
no idea how to govern the kingdom!

82
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:57,790
Every other county would have
considered us a laughingstock!

83
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:04,380
In any case, you have all
toiled for our common goal.

84
00:06:05,010 --> 00:06:06,300
I must thank you.

85
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:07,550
We are unworthy...

86
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:11,180
Without your support, Your Highness,
none of this would have come to pass!

87
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:30,700
Now we have ensured
the preservation of the noble bloodline.

88
00:06:41,210 --> 00:06:42,420
W-What?

89
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:43,420
Is that smoke?

90
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:44,590
It can't be!

91
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:46,420
Open the door!

92
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,010
What's wrong?

93
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:54,560
I-It's locked!

94
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,510
What?

95
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:01,650
Step back from the door!

96
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:10,950
F-Fire!

97
00:07:11,910 --> 00:07:12,780
What is this?

98
00:07:24,590 --> 00:07:26,340
What is this all about?

99
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:44,020
G-Griffith!

100
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,480
Why?

101
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:52,150
The doctor confirmed
that you had perished!

102
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,780
Certainly, it appeared that way to you.

103
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:58,540
Because I arranged things to that end.

104
00:07:58,540 --> 00:07:59,540
What?

105
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:02,750
It was not poison that you saw me drink.

106
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:08,420
It was a secret potion with henbane,
which induced a brief comatose state.

107
00:08:09,090 --> 00:08:12,470
Of course, an overdose
would have killed me...

108
00:08:13,010 --> 00:08:15,090
But it was well worth risking my life...

109
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:20,060
...since I was able to trap
you all in one fell swoop!

110
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,180
H-Help me!

111
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:26,730
I just happened to be summoned
by the queen and Minister Foss!

112
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:29,230
I had nothing to do with it!

113
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:30,940
Hold your tongue, you fool!

114
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:33,070
I suppose you are all...

115
00:08:33,070 --> 00:08:36,280
...too used to sitting at your desks,
thinking up your little plots.

116
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,580
This is a war.

117
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:42,540
There are no grandstands on the battlefield.

118
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,290
You swine, Griffith!

119
00:08:47,290 --> 00:08:49,340
Do you intend to kill me?

120
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:52,710
Do you think that a man...

121
00:08:52,710 --> 00:08:57,470
...of lowly origins like you can burn me,
the queen of the Midland, to death?

122
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,220
I won't allow it!

123
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:01,140
I do not admit defeat!

124
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:05,480
On the battlefield, one does
not die royalty, a nobleman...

125
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,020
...or a commoner.

126
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:09,900
You die as the loser of the battle.

127
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:29,790
It's all over...

128
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,340
What's the matter with you?

129
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:34,090
A man of your stature.

130
00:09:34,510 --> 00:09:37,760
Surely this is not an uncommon
thing to occur within the court.

131
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:40,100
Are you afraid?

132
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,430
Because you betrayed your own comrades?

133
00:09:43,060 --> 00:09:47,690
Or perhaps... because you lent
a hand in murdering the queen?

134
00:09:50,730 --> 00:09:52,690
I'd like to ask you one thing...

135
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:58,530
How did Your Lordship
know about our plot?

136
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:01,700
I didn't know about it.

137
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,740
But then... why did you approach me?

138
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:07,410
I predicted you were going
to become my enemy on that morning...

139
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,880
...before I was last sent to the battlefield.

140
00:10:18,090 --> 00:10:19,340
That was when...

141
00:10:29,390 --> 00:10:31,730
You saw my eyes...

142
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:37,530
And I knew that you would no longer
tolerate my existence in the court.

143
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:41,410
H-How did you...

144
00:10:42,490 --> 00:10:46,700
Because in that moment, I could see
that your eyes were clouded with fear.

145
00:10:48,210 --> 00:10:51,880
When one is confronted by something
he finds to be truly frightening...

146
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,380
...he realizes that it is
impossible to ignore it.

147
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:57,210
In such a situation,
he has one of two choices...

148
00:10:57,710 --> 00:11:01,050
Either to submit to its control,
thereby ensuring his own protection...

149
00:11:01,050 --> 00:11:04,300
...or to annihilate it,
thus eliminating the terror he harbors.

150
00:11:05,310 --> 00:11:10,690
I was aware certain people in the court
were offended by my presence.

151
00:11:11,310 --> 00:11:13,650
I just couldn't pinpoint who they were.

152
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:17,030
But I knew how shrewd of a man you are.

153
00:11:17,030 --> 00:11:21,820
I was certain you'd rally the others
and convince them to eliminate me.

154
00:11:23,740 --> 00:11:28,700
However, I never imagined
the queen would join the intrigue...

155
00:11:29,910 --> 00:11:31,870
This is unbelievable!

156
00:11:31,870 --> 00:11:34,540
His eyes just met mine for a moment!

157
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:39,970
Have I been dancing
to his tune ever since then?

158
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:44,470
Now I know why I can't
stop myself from trembling.

159
00:11:44,470 --> 00:11:49,180
Not because I betrayed my comrades
or took part in the queen's murder.

160
00:11:51,770 --> 00:11:53,400
It's because of this man...

161
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,900
It's because I am terrified of this man!

162
00:11:59,070 --> 00:12:03,280
This contract sealed with your blood...
We can do away with it now, no?

163
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:08,870
There should be no ill will between us
if we are to have a successful future.

164
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:15,710
Hopefully, there will only be peace
and friendship, wouldn't you agree?

165
00:12:19,130 --> 00:12:21,420
Now, come along, Minister...

166
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:23,680
It is time for me to return
something to you, as promised.

167
00:12:24,130 --> 00:12:25,260
Elise!

168
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,720
Father!

169
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:31,310
Thank goodness you're
all right! You're safe now!

170
00:12:31,310 --> 00:12:33,020
Father!

171
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:37,730
Enjoying the poignant reunion scene, sir?

172
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:41,990
Well, abducting her was no small task.

173
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:47,160
We checked that kid's entire
lesson plan a week beforehand...

174
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:49,450
And snatched her as she set off in a carriage.

175
00:12:49,450 --> 00:12:52,540
We treated her courteously while
she was in our care, as you wished.

176
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:54,410
You did a good job.

177
00:12:54,790 --> 00:12:55,870
Here is the rest of your reward...

178
00:12:56,370 --> 00:12:57,710
Oh, great!

179
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:02,670
Anytime you need something,
just let us know.

180
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:08,220
From now on, we only desire
a good relationship with you, sir.

181
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:10,470
Well, we are off.

182
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,900
What a cinch!

183
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:25,360
I've never had such an easy job.
I want to work for him again!

184
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:30,450
No problem... If he ever decides to cut
our connection, we'll blackmail him...

185
00:13:30,450 --> 00:13:33,040
...with the dirt we have!

186
00:13:36,210 --> 00:13:36,750
Who is it?

187
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:40,840
Who the hell are you?

188
00:13:58,560 --> 00:13:59,520
It seems to be finished...

189
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:00,610
Yeah...

190
00:14:01,110 --> 00:14:02,690
...it's taken care of.

191
00:14:02,690 --> 00:14:03,570
Everything.

192
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:10,570
Still, who knew these men would
lose their lives for a handful of coins?

193
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:13,620
Leave the money on them as it was.

194
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:17,620
They earned it, after all.
That's their rightful share.

195
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,250
They did the amount of
work they were paid for.

196
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:23,340
Money opens all doors...

197
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:24,250
...I see.

198
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:29,260
But is it safe to let that man go?

199
00:14:29,930 --> 00:14:32,970
He must have learned his
lesson after today's events...

200
00:14:32,970 --> 00:14:33,720
Maybe...

201
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:34,640
Hey...

202
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:35,560
Maybe?

203
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:38,390
If something happens, I'll take
care of it when the time comes.

204
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:42,400
Still, you can bet there's going
to be another huge uproar over this.

205
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:45,980
So many dead bodies piling up, now
even the queen's. All in just one night.

206
00:14:46,990 --> 00:14:50,280
But no one would imagine that
the man who was supposed to die...

207
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:51,910
...was the one pulling the strings.

208
00:14:53,830 --> 00:14:55,740
Tell me, do you find me vile?

209
00:14:57,750 --> 00:15:00,710
I made you an accomplice
in such a dastardly plot...

210
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:03,590
...while never getting my own hands dirty.

211
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:07,340
I left all of the dangerous
and difficult tasks to you alone...

212
00:15:09,550 --> 00:15:11,890
So tell me, do you think I am a vile man?

213
00:15:14,850 --> 00:15:17,640
You're asking someone who's
slaughtered a hundred men.

214
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,100
Kind of late to be
wondering, don't you think?

215
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:25,110
You're just following this path so
you can realize your dream, right?

216
00:15:25,690 --> 00:15:27,360
You believe that, don't you?

217
00:15:27,690 --> 00:15:29,820
So what's all this you're talking about now?

218
00:15:31,530 --> 00:15:32,820
You're right...

219
00:15:33,030 --> 00:15:35,030
Now, let's go back!

220
00:15:35,030 --> 00:15:37,660
A dead man like you shouldn't
hang around here all night.

221
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:41,580
You've got to keep Casca and
the others from worrying too much.

222
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:42,330
Yeah...

223
00:15:43,250 --> 00:15:48,130
You didn't notice since you were dead,
but Casca wore a dress for the party.

224
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:49,970
Really?

225
00:15:49,970 --> 00:15:52,130
And it was definitely a sight worth seeing!

226
00:16:06,610 --> 00:16:07,480
Gri...

227
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:08,780
...ffith...

228
00:16:13,950 --> 00:16:15,530
Griffith!

229
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:18,740
Griffith!

230
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:22,910
Are you all right?

231
00:16:25,330 --> 00:16:28,000
Griffith, Griffith...

232
00:16:30,130 --> 00:16:32,760
I'm sorry I distressed you, Casca.

233
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:35,090
We had no idea what was going to happen!

234
00:16:35,090 --> 00:16:39,510
Ever since you collapsed,
Casca's been in a state of shock...

235
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,060
I am sorry.

236
00:16:45,270 --> 00:16:47,190
You look pretty in that dress.

237
00:17:31,110 --> 00:17:35,150
Just as the Tudor Empire
conceded to an armistice signing...

238
00:17:35,150 --> 00:17:36,740
Who on earth did this?

239
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:40,530
Perhaps someone who is
plotting against the armistice signing.

240
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:43,200
It must be reactionaries from Tudor!

241
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:47,170
Otherwise, there is the possibility of
an assassin sent by a third country.

242
00:17:47,170 --> 00:17:48,830
How foolish they are...

243
00:17:49,170 --> 00:17:53,000
It is quite unforgivable
to disturb our long-awaited peace...

244
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:05,930
Snow...

245
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:15,440
Guts...

246
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:27,200
And you wouldn't believe
the way that woman was acting!

247
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:31,160
Casca, where are you going this late?

248
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,080
Why is she in such a rush?

249
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:37,290
She's running to the bathroom,
I bet. It's such a cold night...

250
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,800
Guts!

251
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:55,020
Guts...

252
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:56,400
You're...

253
00:20:57,650 --> 00:20:59,730
Are you leaving?

254
00:21:01,190 --> 00:21:02,280
Are you?

255
00:21:04,110 --> 00:21:05,610
Wait a minute.

256
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:08,700
You and I have our differences, but...

257
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:11,580
We've hovered between life and
death together, remember?

258
00:21:12,250 --> 00:21:16,500
All our hard work as the Band of the
Hawk is just starting to bear fruit now.

259
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:19,000
This is just the beginning
for us, don't you see?

260
00:21:19,290 --> 00:21:20,920
So how can you...

261
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:24,260
I've already decided.

262
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:25,800
But...

263
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,840
I don't...

264
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:34,270
I don't want to live
like this, buried in his dream...

265
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

266
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

267
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

268
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

269
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

270
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

271
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

272
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

273
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

274
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

275
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

